{"question_id":"jwpyjNwuJNOyorpKwD1klfg9ziw","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 2 Offline","year":2016,"subject":"physics","chapter":"electrostatics","chapterGroup":"electricity","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":0,"content":"Consider an evacuated cylindrical chamber of height h having rigid conducting plates at the ends and an insulating curved surface as shown in the figure. A number of spherical balls made of a light weight and soft material and coated with a conducting material are placed on the bottom plate. The balls have a radius r &lt;&lt; h. Now, a high voltage source (HV) connected across the conducting plates such that the bottom plate is at +V<sub>0</sub> and the top plate at <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>V<sub>0</sub>. Due to their conducting surface, the balls will get charge, will become equipotential with the plate and are repelled by it. The balls will eventually collide with the top plate, where the coefficient of restitution can be taken to be zero due to the soft nature of the material of the balls. The electric field in the chamber can be considered to be that of a parallel plate capacitor. Assume that there are no collisions between the balls and the interaction between them is negligible. (Ignore gravity)<br><br> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l0nl057l/c319cae6-1c9f-449a-a260-aa91563f59b6/c8a1bd10-a1dd-11ec-8e05-8335d5ab6ad2/file-1l0nl057m.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l0nl057l/c319cae6-1c9f-449a-a260-aa91563f59b6/c8a1bd10-a1dd-11ec-8e05-8335d5ab6ad2/file-1l0nl057m.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Electrostatics Question 39 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l0nl057l/c319cae6-1c9f-449a-a260-aa91563f59b6/c8a1bd10-a1dd-11ec-8e05-8335d5ab6ad2/file-1l0nl057m.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l0nl057l/c319cae6-1c9f-449a-a260-aa91563f59b6/c8a1bd10-a1dd-11ec-8e05-8335d5ab6ad2/file-1l0nl057m.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l0nl057l/c319cae6-1c9f-449a-a260-aa91563f59b6/c8a1bd10-a1dd-11ec-8e05-8335d5ab6ad2/file-1l0nl057m.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l0nl057l/c319cae6-1c9f-449a-a260-aa91563f59b6/c8a1bd10-a1dd-11ec-8e05-8335d5ab6ad2/file-1l0nl057m.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l0nl057l/c319cae6-1c9f-449a-a260-aa91563f59b6/c8a1bd10-a1dd-11ec-8e05-8335d5ab6ad2/file-1l0nl057m.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l0nl057l/c319cae6-1c9f-449a-a260-aa91563f59b6/c8a1bd10-a1dd-11ec-8e05-8335d5ab6ad2/file-1l0nl057m.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"><br>Which one of the following statement is correct? ","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"The balls will execute simple harmonic motion between the two plates"},{"identifier":"B","content":"The balls will bounce back to the bottom plate carrying the same charge they went up with"},{"identifier":"C","content":"The balls will stick to the top plate and remain there"},{"identifier":"D","content":"The balls will bounce back to the bottom plate carrying the opposite charge they went up with"}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>The distance between the two plates is h. The potential of the bottom plate is V<sub>0</sub> and that of the top plates is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>V<sub>0</sub>. The electric field between the plates is E = 2V<sub>0</sub>/h (directed upwards). The radius of each ball is r (&lt;&lt; h). Let m be the mass and C be the capacitance of each ball.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l0ra517z/dce04bb8-83cf-4f5d-a42a-eb405b569b3a/6ec5dff0-a3e6-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0ra5180.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l0ra517z/dce04bb8-83cf-4f5d-a42a-eb405b569b3a/6ec5dff0-a3e6-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0ra5180.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Electrostatics Question 39 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l0ra517z/dce04bb8-83cf-4f5d-a42a-eb405b569b3a/6ec5dff0-a3e6-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0ra5180.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l0ra517z/dce04bb8-83cf-4f5d-a42a-eb405b569b3a/6ec5dff0-a3e6-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0ra5180.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l0ra517z/dce04bb8-83cf-4f5d-a42a-eb405b569b3a/6ec5dff0-a3e6-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0ra5180.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l0ra517z/dce04bb8-83cf-4f5d-a42a-eb405b569b3a/6ec5dff0-a3e6-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0ra5180.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l0ra517z/dce04bb8-83cf-4f5d-a42a-eb405b569b3a/6ec5dff0-a3e6-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0ra5180.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l0ra517z/dce04bb8-83cf-4f5d-a42a-eb405b569b3a/6ec5dff0-a3e6-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0ra5180.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>When the ball touches the bottom plate, it gets a positive charge q = CV<sub>0</sub> (we assume that the charge transfer is instantaneous). This positively charged ball experiences an upward force, F = qE = 2CV<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.687ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"2.573ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.9 436.6 1137.4\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-287.9) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>/h, which accelerates the ball upwards. Since the force is constant, the ball cannot do SHM (for SHM, the force should be proportional to the displacement and directed towards the centre).</p>\n<p>When the ball hits the top plate, it transfers the positive charge to the plate and gets negative charge q = <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>CV<sub>0</sub>. This negatively charged ball again experience a force F = qE (downward) and starts accelerating downwards. Thus, the ball keeps moving between the bottom and the top plates carrying a charge +q upwards and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>q downwards.</p>","qKey":"jwpyjNwuJNOyorpKwD1klfg9ziw","paperKey":"jee-advanced-2016-paper-2-offline","exam":"jee-advanced","questions":[{"question_id":"jwpyjNwuJNOyorpKwD1klfg9ziw","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 2 Offline","year":2016,"subject":"physics","chapter":"electrostatics","chapterGroup":"electricity","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":0,"content":"Consider an evacuated cylindrical chamber of height h having rigid conducting plates at the ends and an insulating curved surface as shown in the figure. A number of spherical balls made of a light weight and soft material and coated with a conducting material are placed on the bottom plate. The balls have a radius r &lt;&lt; h. Now, a high voltage source (HV) connected across the conducting plates such that the bottom plate is at +V<sub>0</sub> and the top plate at <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\